#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The sim's road_edges + Canvas.road must be BIT-IDENTICAL to the firmware C.

Both are fixed-point ports of shared-module/picogame (__init__.c picogame_road_edges,
Canvas.c picogame_canvas_road) - same Q15 sine LUT, same int32 accumulator wrap, same
trunc-toward-zero edge stores. The failure mode of a drifted port is a road that curves
differently in the sim than on the device, which is exactly what the sim exists to prevent.

The vectors below were generated by compiling those two C functions standalone (gcc, host)
and recording inputs -> outputs over seeded pseudo-random cases (seed 777; incl. cases that
overflow the int32 accumulators, so the wrap semantics are covered). The WASM playground
build passes the same vectors. Regenerate by re-extracting the functions from the current C
into a tiny driver if the firmware algorithm ever changes.

    python3 sim/selftest_road.py
"""
